{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.1"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [1], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["LABEL_QUIRK_NO_ARABIC", "SPEAKER_ATTRIBUTION"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-001", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "॥ १ ॥", "sourcePage": {"printed": 1, "scanLeaf": 47}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Dhritarâshtra said :\nOn the holy plain, on the field of Kuru, gathered together, eager for battle, what did they, O Sañjaya, my people and the Pândavas?"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.2"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [2], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["SPEAKER_ATTRIBUTION", "FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-002", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(2)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 2, "scanLeaf": 48}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Sañjaya said :\nHaving seen arrayed the army of the Pândavas, the Râjâ Duryodhana approached his teacher, and spake these words :"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.3"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [3], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-003", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(3)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 2, "scanLeaf": 48}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Behold this mighty host of the sons of Pându, O teacher, arrayed by the son of Drupada, thy wise disciple."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.4"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [4], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-004", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(4)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 2, "scanLeaf": 48}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Heroes are these, mighty bowmen, to Bhîma and Arjuna equal in battle ; Yuyudhâna, Virâta, and Drupada of the great car :"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.5"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [5], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED", "DIACRITIC_COMPLEXITY"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-005", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(5)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 3, "scanLeaf": 49}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Dhrishtaketu, Chekitâna, and the valiant Râjâ of Kâshî ; Purujit and Kuntibhoja, and Shaibya, bull among men ;"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.6"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [6], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-006", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(6)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 3, "scanLeaf": 49}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Yudhâmanyu the strong, and Uttamaujâ the brave ; Saubhadra and the Draupadeyas, all of great cars."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.7"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [7], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-007", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(7)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 4, "scanLeaf": 50}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Know further all those who are our chiefs, O best of the twice-born, the leaders of my army ; these I name to thee for thy information :"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.8"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [8], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED", "DIACRITIC_COMPLEXITY"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-008", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(8)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 4, "scanLeaf": 50}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Thou, lord and Bhîshma, and Karna, and Kripa, conquering in battle ; Ashvatthâmâ, Vikarna, and Saumadatti also ;"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.9"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [9], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-009", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(9)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 5, "scanLeaf": 51}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "And many others, heroes, for my sake renouncing their lives, with divers weapons and missiles, and all well-skilled in war."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.10"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [10], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-010", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(10)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 5, "scanLeaf": 51}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Yet insufficient seems this army of ours, though marshalled by Bhîshma, while that army of theirs seems sufficient, though marshalled by Bhîma;"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.11"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [11], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["QUOTATION_MARK_UNCERTAIN"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-011", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(11)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 5, "scanLeaf": 51}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Therefore in the rank and file let all, standing firmly in their respective divisions, guard Bhîshma, even all ye Generals."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.12"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [12], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-012", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(12)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 6, "scanLeaf": 52}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "To enhearten him, the Ancient of the Kurus, the Grandsire, the glorious, blew his conch, sounding on high a lion's roar."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.13"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [13], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-013", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(13)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 6, "scanLeaf": 52}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Then conches and kettledrums, tabors and drums and cowhorns suddenly blared forth, and the sound was tumultuous."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.14"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [14], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-014", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(14)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 7, "scanLeaf": 53}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Then, stationed in their great war-chariot, yoked to white horses, Mâdhava and the son of Pându blew their divine conches,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.15"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [15], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-015", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(15)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 7, "scanLeaf": 53}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Pânchajanya by Hrishîkesha, and Devadatta by Dhananjaya. Vrikodara, of terrible deeds, blew his mighty conch, Paundra ;"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.16"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [16], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED", "DIACRITIC_COMPLEXITY"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-016", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(16)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 8, "scanLeaf": 54}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "The Râjâ Yudhishthira, the son of Kuntî, blew Anantavijaya ; Nakula and Sahadeva, Sughosha and Manipushpaka."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.17"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [17], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED", "DIACRITIC_COMPLEXITY"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-017", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(17)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 8, "scanLeaf": 54}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "And Kâshya, of the great bow, and Shikhandî, the mighty car-warrior, Dhrishtadyumna and Virâta and Sâtyaki, the unconquered."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.18"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [18], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-018", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(18)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 8, "scanLeaf": 54}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Drupada and the Draupadeyas, O Lord of earth, and Saubhadra, the mighty-armed, on all sides their several conches blew."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.19"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [19], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-019", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(19)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 9, "scanLeaf": 55}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "That tumultuous uproar rent the hearts of the sons of Dhritarâshtra, filling the earth and sky with sound."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.20"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [20], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["CROSS_PAGE_CONTINUATION"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-020", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(20)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 9, "scanLeaf": 55}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Then, beholding the sons of Dhritarâshtra standing arrayed, and the flight of missiles about to begin, he whose crest is an ape, the son of Pându, took up his bow,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.21"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [21], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["SPEAKER_ATTRIBUTION", "CROSS_PAGE_CONTINUATION", "OPEN_QUOTATION_CONTINUES"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-021", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(21)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 10, "scanLeaf": 56}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "And spake this word to Hrishîkesha, O Lord of earth:\nArjuna said :\n\"In the midst, between the two armies, stay my chariot, O Achyuta,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.22"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [22], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["OPEN_QUOTATION_CONTINUES"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-022", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(22)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 10, "scanLeaf": 56}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "That I may behold these standing, longing for battle, with whom I must strive in this out-breaking war ;"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.23"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [23], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["QUOTATION_MARK_UNCERTAIN"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-023", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(23)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 11, "scanLeaf": 57}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "And gaze on those here gathered together, ready to fight, desirous of pleasing in battle the evil-minded son of Dhritarâshtra."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.24"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [24], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["SPEAKER_ATTRIBUTION", "FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED", "DIACRITIC_COMPLEXITY"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-024", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(24)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 11, "scanLeaf": 57}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Sañjaya said :\nThus addressed by Gudâkesha, Hrishîkesha, O Bhârata, having stayed that best of chariots in the midst, between the two armies,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.25"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [25], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-025", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(25)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 12, "scanLeaf": 58}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Over against Bhîshma, Drona and all the rulers of the world, said : \"O Pârtha, behold these Kurus gathered together.\""}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.26"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [26], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-026", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(26)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 12, "scanLeaf": 58}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Then saw Pârtha standing there uncles and grandfathers, teachers, mother's brothers, cousins, sons and grandsons, comrades,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.27"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [27], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["CROSS_PAGE_CONTINUATION", "FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-027", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(27)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 13, "scanLeaf": 59}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Fathers-in-law and friends also in both armies. Seeing all these kinsmen, thus standing arrayed, Kaunteya,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.28"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [28], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["LABEL_QUIRK_NO_ARABIC", "SPEAKER_ATTRIBUTION"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-028", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "॥ २८ ॥", "sourcePage": {"printed": 13, "scanLeaf": 59}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Deeply moved to pity, this uttered in sadness :\nArjuna said :\nSeeing these, my kinsmen, O Krishna, arrayed eager to fight,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.29"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [29], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-029", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(29)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 13, "scanLeaf": 59}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "My limbs fail and my mouth is parched, my body quivers, and my hair stands on end,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.30"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [30], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["DIACRITIC_COMPLEXITY"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-030", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(30)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 14, "scanLeaf": 60}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Gândîva slips from my hand, and my skin burns all over ; I am not able to stand, and my mind is whirling,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.31"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [31], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-031", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(31)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 14, "scanLeaf": 60}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "And I see adverse omens, O Keshava. Nor do I foresee any advantage from slaying kinsmen in battle."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.32"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [32], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-032", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(32)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 15, "scanLeaf": 61}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "For I desire not victory, O Krishna, nor kingdom, nor pleasures ; what is kingdom to us, O Govinda, what enjoyment, or even life ?"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.33"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [33], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["LABEL_QUIRK_NO_ARABIC", "CROSS_PAGE_CONTINUATION"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-033", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "॥ ३३ ॥", "sourcePage": {"printed": 15, "scanLeaf": 61}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Those for whose sake we desire kingdom, enjoyments and pleasures, they stand here in battle, abandoning life and riches—"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.34"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [34], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["CROSS_PAGE_CONTINUATION"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-034", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(34)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 16, "scanLeaf": 62}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Teachers, fathers, sons, as well as grandfathers, mother's brothers, fathers-in-law, grandsons, brothers-in-law, and other relatives."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.35"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [35], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["DIACRITIC_COMPLEXITY"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-035", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(35)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 16, "scanLeaf": 62}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "These I do not wish to kill, though myself slain, O Madhusûdana, even for the sake of the kingship of the three worlds; how then for earth?"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.36"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [36], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-036", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(36)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 16, "scanLeaf": 62}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Slaying these sons of Dhritarâshtra, what pleasure can be ours, O Janârdana? killing these desperadoes sin will but take hold of us."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.37"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [37], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-037", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(37)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 17, "scanLeaf": 63}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Therefore we should not kill the sons of Dhritarâshtra, our relatives ; for how, killing our kinsmen, may we be happy, O Mâdhava ?"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.38"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [38], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-038", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(38)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 17, "scanLeaf": 63}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Although these, with intelligence overpowered by greed, see no guilt in the destruction of a family, no crime in hostility to friends,"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.39"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [39], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-039", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(39)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 18, "scanLeaf": 64}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Why should not we learn to turn away from such a sin, O Janârdana, who see the evils in the destruction of a family?"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.40"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [40], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["FOOTNOTE_MARKER_STRIPPED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-040", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(40)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 18, "scanLeaf": 64}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "In the destruction of a family the immemorial family traditions perish ; in the perishing of traditions lawlessness overcomes the whole family ;"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.41"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [41], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["DIACRITIC_COMPLEXITY"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-041", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(41)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 19, "scanLeaf": 65}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Owing to predominance of lawlessness, O Krishna, the women of the family become corrupt; women corrupted, O Vârshneya, there ariseth caste-confusion;"}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.42"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [42], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-042", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(42)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 19, "scanLeaf": 65}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "This confusion draggeth to hell the slayers of the family and the family ; for their ancestors fall, deprived of rice-balls and libations."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.43"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [43], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["CROSS_PAGE_CONTINUATION"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-043", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(43)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 20, "scanLeaf": 66}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "By these caste-confusing misdeeds of the slayers of the family, the everlasting caste customs and family customs are abolished."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.44"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [44], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["ITALICS_PRESENTATION_DEFERRED"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-044", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(44)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 20, "scanLeaf": 66}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "The abode of the men whose family customs are extinguished, O Janârdana, is everlastingly in hell. Thus have we heard."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.45"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [45], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-045", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(45)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 20, "scanLeaf": 66}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Alas! in committing a great sin are we engaged, we who are endeavouring to kill our kindred from greed of the pleasures of kingship."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.46"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [46], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": [], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-046", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(46)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 21, "scanLeaf": 67}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "If the sons of Dhritarâshtra, weapon-in-hand, should slay me, unresisting, unarmed, in the battle, that would for me be the better."}
{"chapterNumber": 1, "contentVersion": 1, "coveredCanonicalReferences": ["1.47"], "coveredVerseNumbers": [47], "editorialNotes": [], "language": "en", "provider": "Annie Besant & Bhagavan Das", "publicationStatus": "UNREVIEWED", "reviewFlags": ["SPEAKER_ATTRIBUTION"], "segmentId": "besant-das-1905-bg-1-047", "sourceChecksum": "7fb78b0a6b004f195c3ca61c091501084e553627c51cde1c309f2d0620ea6115", "sourceId": "bhagavad-gita-translation-en-besant-das-1905-v1", "sourceLabel": "(47)", "sourcePage": {"printed": 21, "scanLeaf": 67}, "sourceRole": "PRIMARY_TRANSLATION_CANDIDATE", "translationText": "Sañjaya said :\nHaving thus spoken on the battle-field, Arjuna sank down on the seat of the chariot, casting away his bow and arrow, his mind overborne by grief."}
